Creator Flow — the node-based generation canvas at /creator/flow
(src/pages/app/CreatorFlowPage.tsx, src/pages/app/CreatorFlowPublicPage.tsx,
src/components/app/creator/flow/*, src/lib/creator/flow/*,
src/store/creatorFlowStore.ts, src/store/creatorFolderStore.ts, and the
creator-flows and creator-prompt-assistant edge functions) — is adapted from
HeliosGen (https://github.com/segfault42/heliosgen), an open-source visual
pipeline builder for AI image and video generation released under the MIT
license.

The graph model (spaces of nodes and edges with per-type counters), the
execution helpers (topological order, parallel waves, upstream input
resolution, @mention ordering of reference images), the store shape with
undo/redo and inherited node defaults, the debounced database sync with
immediate flush on discrete edits, the folder store, the public read-only
viewer, the alignment snapping, copy/paste and edge-drop node picker on the
canvas, and the prompt-crafting assistant persona are derived from that
project. The implementation has been re-written for this Vite + React +
Supabase stack: DeHub's own model catalogue, wallet-native auth and per-job
DHB payment replace HeliosGen's Next.js API routes and kie.ai credits, frame
capture runs in the browser instead of ffmpeg, and the styling follows DeHub's
monochrome design system.

